,1).$\n\n- For the scaled function $y=1.5({10}^{x}),$ the $y$-coordinate becomes\n\n$$\ny=1.5\\cdot 1=1.5.\n$$\n\n- Finally, after a vertical shift of $8.5$ units down, we get a point with the $y$-coordinate\n\n$$\ny=1.5-8.5=-7.\n$$\n\n**Method 2** \n\nTo find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1.5({10}^{0})-8.5 \\\\  & =1.5\\cdot 1-8.5 \\\\  & =1.5-8.5 \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=1.5({10}^{x})-8.5$ intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-30873/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "40eeb5a8-3ffe-54d2-b263-f2b1c41fed93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-30873"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7121/selection/aea163e3a624450f57351f4dbb392c0a29c4a949863f811a2aeadb53828d3354" :answer/id #uuid "7941b161-26ae-598c-a669-dc9a40eceee0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930907/assets/752c0102b1c019f5bc13673b0107627bf58954fb5ef5b80d3b43e33e5f46f55d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7121/selection/98c5e482884d1a2eac8e67c03329e625f95c1f567762a68dc988d670ba3131a5" :answer/id #uuid "2673e6f6-6cc5-5ef8-84bb-0f66fe92cb9f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930907/assets/eed5f150b826a708834eb9d7c4595cbdcc0113842fc0b172c1cf11e65681b199.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7121/selection/a8cf9b311152d73c20552a7ad3af082c5cde621b1cb4e6e64fec3ed5374706b9" :answer/id #uuid "cb744e0b-4ee6-5415-ab50-f3e815f4d529" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930907/assets/d5c68724af1732ee023599ce2969c165dfc68b8e198e14cebbc1262bbf1bd881.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7121/selection/fa629